A||||4||Alex2004||Where i splice the PONTIAC lights at?||||5||
Z||000000||Alex2004||01-03-2001||05:03 PM||||I have an 84 SE with an 86 GT fast back and tail lights.  Just wondering where to splice them in at so they are on when the car is on. Let me know, thanks.... Alex...||||reg||5
Z||000001||lawrence||01-03-2001||07:42 PM||||I'm looking at the Helms manual for my 88GT.  The circuit shows a connection at connector C500 (the large one behind the battery).  Assuming you have one of those, the contact G8 should go up to the fuse that controls the fan.  Fan power is avaiable when you turn on the car.<P>Put a voltmeter from G8 to ground and turn on the car and see if you have +12 or so there.  Then remove the fan fuse (marked E in this book) and see if the power drops.  If so, then you can simply connect here.<P>Good luck,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://www.webelectricmagazine.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.webelectricmagazine.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||01-03-2001||07:49 PM||||If you don't have the C-500 block in the car, ('84's stock dosn't have one), run a wire to the fuse block and put an inline fuse in it (5 amp, maybe 10 at most) and tie (plug in) into an ingnition terminal there.<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 01-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex2004||01-03-2001||09:55 PM||||So you are saying to splice into the ingnition wire at the fuse block.......right???||||reg||5
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||01-03-2001||11:19 PM||||No, not into the iginition 'wire' itself, but to a terminial (like the one in the lower left hand corner) of the fuse block.||||reg||1
